                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div><span>Pathophysiology is a "bridge subject" that connects basic medicine and clinical medicine, mainly including the causes, basic mechanisms and rules of disease occurrence and development, basic pathological processes, and pathophysiology of various system organs. Through theoretical learning and experiments, the students are able to understand the general laws of disease occurrence, development and prognosis, comprehend the mechanisms of pathological processes and the intrinsic connections between functional and metabolic changes and clinical manifestations, that will lay a solid foundation for future clinical medicine studies.</span></div></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
